<p>Leo Charles Broderick was born in Winona, Minnesota on December 27, 1884 to Michael and Anna (Quinn) Broderick. He graduated from the Winona High School. However, upon his father's death in 1902, his mother moved the family to Minneapolis to a home just off University Avenue. The exposure to the city and the University area would resurface later in his life. Leo taught himself shorthand and typing and searched for a clerk position. He initially came to Mandan in 1907 and found a job as a court reporter for district Judge Harry L. Berry who presided over most of the southwest part of the state.</p>

